/**
 * Calculates the nth Fibonacci number.
 *
 * @param {number} n The position of the Fibonacci number to calculate (0-indexed).
 * @returns {number} The nth Fibonacci number.
 * @throws {Error} If n is a negative number.
 *
 * Example usage:
 * const fib = fibonacci(10); // Calculates the 10th Fibonacci number
 */
function fibonacci(n) {
    // Base case: If n is less than or equal to 1, return n directly
    if (n <= 1) return n;

    // Recursive case: If n is greater than 1, calculate the nth Fibonacci number
    // by recursively calculating the (n-1)th and (n-2)th Fibonacci numbers and adding them together
    // This is based on the Fibonacci sequence definition: each number is the sum of the two preceding ones
    return fibonacci(n - 1) + fibonacci(n - 2);
}
